('248', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'career', '{\"ids\":[\"6\",\"5\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\",\"1\"],\"bulk_action\":1,\"bulk_action_table\":\"ArchiElite\\\\Career\\\\Tables\\\\CareerTable\",\"bulk_action_target\":\"Botble\\\\Table\\\\BulkActions\\\\DeleteBulkAction\"}', 'deleted', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '127.0.0.1', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', '4', 'UX/UI Designer, User Experience Team', 'danger', '2026-08-16 16:05:00', '2026-08-16 16:05:00'),
('249', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'career', '{\"ids\":[\"6\",\"5\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\",\"1\"],\"bulk_action\":1,\"bulk_action_table\":\"ArchiElite\\\\Career\\\\Tables\\\\CareerTable\",\"bulk_action_target\":\"Botble\\\\Table\\\\BulkActions\\\\DeleteBulkAction\"}', 'deleted', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '127.0.0.1', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', '5', 'Operations Manager, Supply Chain Division', 'danger', '2026-08-16 16:05:00', '2026-08-16 16:05:00'),
('250', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'career', '{\"ids\":[\"6\",\"5\",\"4\",\"3\",\"2\",\"1\"],\"bulk_action\":1,\"bulk_action_table\":\"ArchiElite\\\\Career\\\\Tables\\\\CareerTable\",\"bulk_action_target\":\"Botble\\\\Table\\\\BulkActions\\\\DeleteBulkAction\"}', 'deleted', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '127.0.0.1', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', '6', 'Financial Analyst, Investment Group', 'danger', '2026-08-16 16:05:00', '2026-08-16 16:05:00'),
('251', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', 'page', '{\"name\":\"Privacy Policy\",\"model\":\"Botble\\\\Page\\\\Models\\\\Page\",\"slug\":\"privacy-policy\",\"slug_id\":\"129\",\"is_slug_editable\":\"1\",\"description\":\"We may collect information that you voluntarily provide to us through our website, contact forms, telephone inquiries, WhatsApp, or other communication channels.\",\"content\":\"<h1>Privacy Policy<\\/h1><p><strong>Last Updated: August 16, 2026<\\/strong><\\/p><p>Green Alliance Enterprises (\\u201cGAE\\u201d, \\u201cwe\\u201d, \\u201cour\\u201d, or \\u201cus\\u201d) respects the privacy of visitors, customers, traders, investors, commission agents, and other users of our website.<\\/p><p>This Privacy Policy explains how we may collect, use, protect, and handle information when you visit our website, contact us, submit an inquiry, request information about commercial shops, or interact with Green Alliance Enterprises.<\\/p><p>By using this website, you acknowledge the practices described in this Privacy Policy.<\\/p><h2>1. Information We May Collect<\\/h2><p>We may collect information that you voluntarily provide to us through our website, contact forms, telephone inquiries, WhatsApp, or other communication channels.<\\/p><p>This information may include:<\\/p><ul><li>Full name<\\/li><li>Phone number<\\/li><li>Email address, if provided<\\/li><li>City or location<\\/li><li>Business or company name<\\/li><li>Nature of your business<\\/li><li>Investment or shop requirements<\\/li><li>Preferred shop size or category<\\/li><li>Messages and inquiries submitted through the website<\\/li><li>Any other information you choose to provide<\\/li><\\/ul><p>We only request information that is reasonably required to respond to your inquiry or provide relevant information about Green Alliance Enterprises.<\\/p><h2>2. Information Collected Automatically<\\/h2><p>When you visit our website, certain technical information may be collected automatically by our website, hosting provider, analytics services, or similar technologies.<\\/p><p>This may include:<\\/p><ul><li>IP address<\\/li><li>Browser type<\\/li><li>Device type<\\/li><li>Operating system<\\/li><li>Pages visited<\\/li><li>Date and time of visits<\\/li><li>Referring website<\\/li><li>General website usage information<\\/li><\\/ul><p>This information may be used to understand website performance, improve the visitor experience, maintain security, and identify technical issues.<\\/p><h2>3. How We Use Your Information<\\/h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may use information collected through the website to:<\\/p><ul><li>Respond to your questions and inquiries<\\/li><li>Provide information about available commercial shops or plots<\\/li><li>Explain booking, allotment, payment, or installment options<\\/li><li>Contact potential investors or customers who request information<\\/li><li>Provide information about Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market<\\/li><li>Communicate with wholesalers, commission agents, retailers, and business owners<\\/li><li>Arrange site visits or meetings when requested<\\/li><li>Improve our website and customer experience<\\/li><li>Maintain website security<\\/li><li>Keep internal records of customer inquiries<\\/li><li>Send relevant project updates where you have requested or consented to receive them<\\/li><\\/ul><p>We do not intend to use personal information for purposes unrelated to your interaction with Green Alliance Enterprises without an appropriate reason or consent.<\\/p><h2>4. Investment and Commercial Shop Inquiries<\\/h2><p>Visitors may contact Green Alliance Enterprises through the website regarding commercial plots, shops, investment opportunities, payment plans, possession, or other project-related matters.<\\/p><p>Information provided through an online inquiry is used primarily to:<\\/p><ul><li>Understand your requirements<\\/li><li>Contact you regarding available opportunities<\\/li><li>Provide relevant project information<\\/li><li>Arrange further discussion with our representatives<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Submitting an inquiry through this website does <strong>not itself constitute a booking, allotment, sale agreement, investment agreement, or legal commitment<\\/strong>.<\\/p><p>Any commercial transaction is subject to the official application forms, allotment documents, payment schedules, terms and conditions, and agreements issued by Green Alliance Enterprises.<\\/p><h2>5. Cookies<\\/h2><p>Our website may use cookies and similar technologies to improve functionality and understand how visitors use the website.<\\/p><p>Cookies are small files stored on your device that may help with:<\\/p><ul><li>Website functionality<\\/li><li>Remembering preferences<\\/li><li>Measuring website traffic<\\/li><li>Understanding visitor behaviour<\\/li><li>Improving website performance<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Where applicable, you may disable or manage cookies through your browser settings. Disabling certain cookies may affect some website features.<\\/p><h2>6. Analytics and Third-Party Services<\\/h2><p>We may use third-party services for website hosting, analytics, security, forms, maps, social-media integration, or other website functionality.<\\/p><p>These service providers may process limited technical information as necessary to provide their services.<\\/p><p>Where third-party services are used, their handling of information may also be governed by their own privacy policies and terms.<\\/p><h2>7. How We Share Information<\\/h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises does not intend to sell or rent visitors\\u2019 personal information to unrelated third parties for their independent marketing purposes.<\\/p><p>Information may, however, be shared where reasonably necessary with:<\\/p><ul><li>Authorized Green Alliance Enterprises staff<\\/li><li>Sales or customer-support representatives<\\/li><li>Service providers supporting our website<\\/li><li>Professional advisers where required<\\/li><li>Government departments, regulators, courts, or authorities where disclosure is legally required<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Information will only be shared where there is a legitimate operational, contractual, security, or legal reason to do so.<\\/p><h2>8. Data Security<\\/h2><p>We take reasonable administrative and technical measures to protect information submitted through our website against unauthorized access, misuse, loss, alteration, or disclosure.<\\/p><p>However, no internet-based transmission or electronic storage method can be guaranteed to be completely secure.<\\/p><p>Visitors should therefore avoid sending highly confidential or sensitive information through ordinary website forms unless specifically requested through an appropriate secure process.<\\/p><h2>9. Data Retention<\\/h2><p>We may retain personal information for as long as reasonably necessary to:<\\/p><ul><li>Respond to inquiries<\\/li><li>Maintain business records<\\/li><li>Manage ongoing customer or investor relationships<\\/li><li>Fulfil contractual obligations<\\/li><li>Resolve disputes<\\/li><li>Meet legal or regulatory requirements<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Information that is no longer reasonably required may be deleted, anonymized, or securely archived where appropriate.<\\/p><h2>10. Your Choices and Requests<\\/h2><p>You may contact Green Alliance Enterprises if you wish to:<\\/p><ul><li>Ask what personal information you have provided to us<\\/li><li>Request correction of inaccurate information<\\/li><li>Request deletion of information where appropriate<\\/li><li>Withdraw consent for optional marketing communications<\\/li><li>Ask questions about how your information is being handled<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Certain information may need to be retained where required for contractual, accounting, regulatory, security, or legal purposes.<\\/p><h2>11. Marketing Communications<\\/h2><p>Where you have requested information about Green Alliance Enterprises, we may contact you regarding:<\\/p><ul><li>Commercial shop availability<\\/li><li>Investment opportunities<\\/li><li>Market development updates<\\/li><li>Payment or installment information<\\/li><li>Project announcements<\\/li><li>Relevant business opportunities<\\/li><\\/ul><p>You may ask us to stop sending optional promotional communications at any time.<\\/p><p>Essential communications relating to an existing booking, allotment, payment, agreement, or business relationship may still need to be sent.<\\/p><h2>12. WhatsApp, Phone and Social Media<\\/h2><p>Our website may provide links or buttons allowing visitors to contact Green Alliance Enterprises through telephone, WhatsApp, Facebook, or other third-party platforms.<\\/p><p>When you use an external platform, information may also be processed according to that platform\'s own privacy policy.<\\/p><p>Green Alliance Enterprises is not responsible for the privacy practices of independent third-party platforms.<\\/p><h2>13. Third-Party Links<\\/h2><p>Our website may contain links to external websites or services.<\\/p><p>We are not responsible for the content, security, or privacy practices of websites operated by third parties.<\\/p><p>Visitors should review the privacy policies of external websites before providing personal information to them.<\\/p><h2>14. Children\'s Privacy<\\/h2><p>This website is intended primarily for adults seeking information about wholesale trading, commercial businesses, shops, and investment opportunities.<\\/p><p>We do not knowingly seek to collect personal information from children for commercial investment purposes.<\\/p><p>If we become aware that information has been submitted by a child where parental or guardian involvement is required, appropriate steps may be taken to remove or otherwise handle that information.<\\/p><h2>15. Accuracy of Information Submitted<\\/h2><p>Visitors are responsible for providing accurate and up-to-date information when submitting inquiries through the website.<\\/p><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may contact users using the telephone number, email address, or other contact details they voluntarily provide.<\\/p><h2>16. Changes to This Privacy Policy<\\/h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may update this Privacy Policy periodically to reflect changes in:<\\/p><ul><li>Website functionality<\\/li><li>Business operations<\\/li><li>Services<\\/li><li>Technology<\\/li><li>Security practices<\\/li><li>Legal or regulatory requirements<\\/li><\\/ul><p>Any updated version will be published on this page with a revised \\u201cLast Updated\\u201d date.<\\/p><p>We encourage visitors to review this Privacy Policy periodically.<\\/p><h2>17. Contact Green Alliance Enterprises<\\/h2><p>If you have questions about this Privacy Policy or how information submitted through our website is handled, please contact us:<\\/p><p><strong>Green Alliance Enterprises<\\/strong><br>Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market<br><strong>Address:<\\/strong> Abbasia Chowk, 0.5 KM towards Bahawalpur Road, Opposite Javed CNG Pump, Ahmedpur East, Punjab, Pakistan<br><strong>Phone:<\\/strong> 0303-3341200<\\/p><p>You may also contact us through the contact form available on our website.<\\/p><h2>Consent<\\/h2><p>By using this website and voluntarily providing your information, you acknowledge that you have read this Privacy Policy and understand how Green Alliance Enterprises may handle information in accordance with the purposes described above.<\\/p>\",\"seo_meta\":{\"seo_title\":null,\"seo_description\":null,\"index\":\"index\"},\"seo_meta_image\":null,\"submitter\":\"apply\",\"status\":\"published\",\"template\":\"default\",\"image\":null,\"breadcrumb\":\"yes\",\"breadcrumb_background_color\":\"transparent\",\"breadcrumb_text_color\":\"transparent\",\"breadcrumb_background_image\":null}', 'updated', 'Mozilla/5.0 (Windows NT 10.0; Win64; x64) AppleWebKit/537.36 (KHTML, like Gecko) Chrome/151.0.0.0 Safari/537.36', '127.0.0.1', '1', 'Botble\\ACL\\Models\\User', '12', 'Privacy Policy', 'primary', '2026-08-16 17:02:03', '2026-08-16 17:02:03'),
