('16', 'Cookie Policy', '<h3>EU Cookie Consent</h3><p>To use this website we are using Cookies and collecting some Data. To be compliant with the EU GDPR we give you to choose if you allow us to use certain Cookies and to collect some Data.</p><h4>Essential Data</h4><p>The Essential Data is needed to run the Site you are visiting technically. You can not deactivate them.</p><p>- Session Cookie: PHP uses a Cookie to identify user sessions. Without this Cookie the Website is not working.</p><p>- XSRF-Token Cookie: Laravel automatically generates a CSRF \"token\" for each active user session managed by the application. This token is used to verify that the authenticated user is the one actually making the requests to the application.</p>', '1', NULL, NULL, NULL, 'published', '2026-05-29 08:48:47', '2026-05-29 08:48:47'),
('17', 'Terms &amp; Conditions', '<h1>Terms &amp; Conditions</h1><p><strong>Last Updated: August 16, 2026</strong></p><p>Welcome to the official website of <strong>Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market (“GAE”)</strong>.</p><p>These Terms &amp; Conditions govern the use of this website and provide general information regarding commercial plot allotment, payments, possession, development, transfers and market operations at Green Alliance Enterprises.</p><p>By using this website, submitting an inquiry, applying for allotment or entering into a transaction with Green Alliance Enterprises, you acknowledge that you have read and understood these Terms &amp; Conditions.</p><h2>1. About Green Alliance Enterprises</h2><p>The project is known as <strong>Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market</strong>, an agricultural wholesale market project located at:</p><p><strong>Abbasia Chowk, approximately 0.5 KM towards Bahawalpur Road, opposite Javed CNG Pump, Ahmedpur East, Punjab, Pakistan.</strong></p><p>The project documentation identifies the market as <strong>approved by PAMRA – Punjab Agricultural Marketing Regulatory Authority</strong>.</p><p>The market is being developed to accommodate commission agents, wholesalers, retailers, traders and supporting commercial businesses.</p><h2>2. Purpose of This Website</h2><p>This website provides general information about:</p><ul><li>Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market</li><li>Commercial plots and business opportunities</li><li>Market infrastructure and facilities</li><li>Payment and installment options</li><li>Possession information</li><li>Investment opportunities</li><li>Market-related services</li><li>Contact and project information</li></ul><p>Information provided on this website is for general guidance and promotional purposes.</p><p>Website content does not by itself constitute an allotment, booking confirmation, sale agreement, lease, transfer, ownership document or legally binding investment agreement.</p><h2>3. Official Documents Take Priority</h2><p>Every allotment or purchase is governed by the official:</p><ul><li>Application Form</li><li>Allotment Letter</li><li>Payment Schedule</li><li>Possession Documents</li><li>Lease or ownership documents</li><li>Project Terms &amp; Conditions</li><li>Company bylaws</li><li>Applicable PAMRA and government rules</li></ul><p>If there is any inconsistency between information displayed on this website and a signed official document issued by Green Alliance Enterprises, the <strong>official signed document shall take priority</strong>.</p><h2>4. Eligibility for Allotment</h2><p>Commercial plots are offered to:</p><ul><li>Commission agents</li><li>Traders and wholesalers</li><li>Business owners</li><li>Investors</li><li>Members of the general public</li></ul><p>Allotments are subject to availability and are generally made on a <strong>first-come, first-served basis</strong>.</p><p>The developer reserves the right to accept, reject or process applications according to project requirements, availability and applicable rules.</p><h2>5. Confirmation of Plot Details</h2><p>At the time of allotment, relevant details may include:</p><ul><li>Plot number</li><li>Plot area</li><li>Total price</li><li>Payment schedule</li><li>Applicable commitments or conditions</li><li>Any other relevant allotment information</li></ul><p>These details become part of the contractual arrangement between the allottee and Green Alliance Enterprises when confirmed through the appropriate official documents.</p><h2>6. Payment Options</h2><p>Depending on the applicable payment schedule, commercial plots may be offered through:</p><ul><li>Cash payment</li><li>Monthly installments</li><li>Quarterly installments</li><li>Other approved installment arrangements</li></ul><p>The exact payment plan applicable to an allottee will be stated in the official payment schedule issued by Green Alliance Enterprises.</p><h2>7. Payment of Installments</h2><p>Allottees are responsible for paying installments strictly according to the agreed payment schedule.</p><p>Green Alliance Enterprises is not required to issue repeated reminders for scheduled payments.</p><p>Timely payment of installments is an essential condition of allotment.</p><h2>8. Late Payment Charges</h2><p>According to the current project Terms &amp; Conditions, delayed installments may be accepted together with outstanding arrears and may be subject to a <strong>late-payment fine calculated at 5% per month for the period of delay</strong>.</p><p>Where installments remain unpaid for the period specified in the official allotment terms, the cancellation process may be initiated.</p><p>Allottees should therefore carefully follow their individual payment schedules.</p><h2>9. Possession After 25% Payment</h2><p>One of the key features of the Green Alliance Enterprises payment plan is the possibility of receiving possession after payment of <strong>25% of the total amount of the allotted plot</strong>, subject to the applicable project terms and requirements.</p><p>A <strong>possession slip</strong> will be issued to the allottee when possession is formally delivered.</p><p>Possession shall only be considered officially transferred when completed through the prescribed process and documentation.</p><h2>10. Taking Possession After Intimation</h2><p>Where Green Alliance Enterprises issues a formal possession intimation after obtaining the required completion documentation from the relevant authority, the allottee is required to take possession within the time period stated in the official project Terms &amp; Conditions.</p><p>The current terms provide a period of <strong>15 days from receipt of the possession intimation</strong>.</p><p>Where possession is delayed by the allottee beyond the applicable period, the current project terms provide for a <strong>caretaking charge of Rs. 1,000 per month</strong>.</p><h2>11. Development Facilities</h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises is responsible for development of specified common infrastructure according to the project terms and approved development plan.</p><p>Planned/developed facilities include:</p><ul><li>Sewerage infrastructure</li><li>Internal roads</li><li>Boundary wall</li><li>Auction platforms</li><li>Electricity infrastructure</li><li>Street lights</li><li>Mosque</li><li>Toilet block</li><li>Other specified common development facilities</li></ul><p>Development remains subject to approved plans, applicable authority requirements and technical considerations.</p><h2>12. Electricity Connections and Related Charges</h2><p>While common electricity infrastructure forms part of project development, individual allottees may be responsible for additional charges relating to:</p><ul><li>Electricity connections</li><li>Electricity meters</li><li>Betterment charges</li><li>External development charges</li><li>Departmental connection charges</li><li>Other charges imposed by the relevant authorities</li></ul><p>Such charges may be payable separately when demanded.</p><h2>13. Government and Authority Charges</h2><p>Certain government, regulatory or departmental charges may not be included in the basic price of the allotted plot.</p><p>The allottee may be responsible for applicable:</p><ul><li>Government charges</li><li>Taxes</li><li>Registration charges</li><li>Licence fees</li><li>Documentation charges</li><li>Lease charges</li><li>Connection charges</li><li>Betterment charges</li><li>Other statutory or departmental fees</li></ul><p>Applicable charges shall be payable according to official requirements and project documentation.</p><h2>14. Documentation and Lease Formalities</h2><p>Allottees are required to cooperate with Green Alliance Enterprises in completing necessary documentation, registration, lease and other legal formalities.</p><p>Documentation and related departmental expenses may be payable separately by the allottee where specified.</p><p>Until the required ownership or lease documentation has been properly completed, rights relating to sale, mortgage, encumbrance or transfer may remain restricted according to the official allotment agreement.</p><h2>15. Construction and Plot Restrictions</h2><p>An allottee must use and develop the allotted area according to:</p><ul><li>Approved plans</li><li>Company bylaws</li><li>PAMRA requirements</li><li>Local government requirements</li><li>Other applicable authority rules</li></ul><p>No construction or projection may extend outside the allotted plot area.</p><p>According to the current project terms, the <strong>plinth level should be approximately 12 inches above road level</strong>.</p><p>All construction must comply with applicable project specifications and bylaws.</p><h2>16. Approved Layout and Plot Demarcation</h2><p>Development of the land shall be carried out according to the approved layout plan and applicable specifications of the relevant authorities.</p><p>Where required by final demarcation, regulatory requirements or an approved revised layout plan, adjustments may be made to:</p><ul><li>Plot numbering</li><li>Plot dimensions</li><li>Plot area</li><li>Layout configuration</li></ul><p>Such matters will be handled according to the official project agreement and applicable authority requirements.</p><h2>17. Transfer or Sale of an Allotted Plot</h2><p>An allottee may not transfer or sell an allotted plot before taking possession without the <strong>prior written permission of Green Alliance Enterprises</strong>.</p><p>Where a transfer is permitted, the developer may require:</p><ul><li>Clearance of outstanding plot payments</li><li>Completion of required documentation</li><li>Payment of the applicable transfer fee</li><li>Compliance with company and authority requirements</li></ul><p>According to the current project Terms &amp; Conditions, the stated transfer/documentation fee is <strong>Rs. 100,000</strong>, subject to the applicable agreement and any subsequent authorized revision.</p><h2>18. Withdrawal and Refund of Allotment</h2><p>An allottee wishing to withdraw from an allotment must follow the formal cancellation procedure and submit the required documents, which may include:</p><ul><li>Original Letter of Allocation</li><li>Original payment receipts</li><li>Written application for withdrawal</li><li>Other documents required by the developer</li></ul><p>According to the current project terms, where an allottee voluntarily withdraws, the developer may refund the payable amount <strong>within up to two years after deduction of 20% of the amount paid as establishment/service charges</strong>.</p><p>The official Terms &amp; Conditions also contain provisions concerning the method and timing of refund payments.</p><p>Because individual circumstances may differ, allottees should review their signed allotment documents before requesting withdrawal.</p><h2>19. Market Fees for Commission Agents</h2><p>Commission agents operating inside Green Alliance Enterprises may be required to pay applicable <strong>market fees in accordance with PAMRA rules and regulations</strong>.</p><p>Fees may vary according to applicable regulations and authority requirements.</p><h2>20. Registration and Licence Requirements</h2><p>Commission agents, pharryaas and other market functionaries are responsible for complying with applicable:</p><ul><li>PAMRA regulations</li><li>Government regulations</li><li>Registration requirements</li><li>Licence requirements</li><li>Taxes</li><li>Market operating rules</li></ul><p>Any required registration or licence fees shall be payable by the relevant market functionary according to authority rules.</p><h2>21. Entry and Parking Charges</h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may charge:</p><ul><li>Vehicle entry fees</li><li>Parking charges</li></ul><p>for vehicles entering or using the market facilities.</p><p>Applicable rates may be determined or revised by market management where permitted.</p><h2>22. Market Rules and Conduct</h2><p>All commission agents, wholesalers, retailers, workers, pharryaas, transporters, visitors and other market participants are required to comply with:</p><ul><li>Green Alliance Enterprises market rules</li><li>Company bylaws</li><li>PAMRA rules and regulations</li><li>Government requirements</li><li>Security procedures</li><li>Parking and traffic rules</li><li>Health and cleanliness requirements</li><li>Other applicable laws or authority instructions</li></ul><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may take reasonable steps to maintain security, cleanliness, traffic management and orderly market operations.</p><h2>23. Use of Market Facilities</h2><p>Common market facilities must be used responsibly.</p><p>Users must not:</p><ul><li>Damage market infrastructure</li><li>Obstruct roads or access points without authorization</li><li>Interfere with auction operations</li><li>Misuse common facilities</li><li>Engage in unlawful activity</li><li>Violate applicable market or authority rules</li></ul><p>The company reserves the right to take appropriate action against violations in accordance with applicable rules.</p><h2>24. Accuracy of Website Information</h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises makes reasonable efforts to keep website information accurate and updated.</p><p>However:</p><ul><li>Prices may change</li><li>Plot availability may change</li><li>Payment schedules may be revised</li><li>Development specifications may be updated</li><li>Government or regulatory charges may change</li><li>Market rules and authority requirements may be amended</li></ul><p>Users should therefore obtain the <strong>latest official price list, payment schedule and Terms &amp; Conditions directly from Green Alliance Enterprises before making any payment or investment decision</strong>.</p><h2>25. Images, Maps and Illustrations</h2><p>Photographs, architectural visuals, maps, layouts, renderings and other promotional material displayed on the website may be used for information and presentation purposes.</p><p>Where a visual is conceptual or illustrative, it should not be treated as a substitute for the officially approved layout, physical site inspection or contractual specifications.</p><p>Prospective buyers are encouraged to review official documents and visit the project site before making a decision.</p><h2>26. No Guarantee of Business Profit</h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises provides commercial infrastructure and business opportunities but does not guarantee:</p><ul><li>Business profits</li><li>Rental income</li><li>Resale value</li><li>Future appreciation</li><li>Customer traffic</li><li>Individual business performance</li><li>Specific investment returns</li></ul><p>Every buyer, trader or investor is responsible for evaluating their own financial position, business requirements and investment decision.</p><h2>27. Website Intellectual Property</h2><p>Unless otherwise stated, website content belonging to Green Alliance Enterprises—including text, branding, graphics, logos, photographs, designs and promotional material—may not be copied, reproduced or used commercially without authorization.</p><h2>28. Third-Party Links and Services</h2><p>The website may include links or integrations involving third-party services such as:</p><ul><li>Google Maps</li><li>WhatsApp</li><li>Social media platforms</li><li>Banks</li><li>External websites</li></ul><p>Green Alliance Enterprises is not responsible for the independent content, availability, privacy practices or terms of third-party services.</p><h2>29. Privacy</h2><p>Personal information submitted through this website will be handled in accordance with the <strong>Green Alliance Enterprises Privacy Policy</strong>.</p><p>Visitors should review the Privacy Policy to understand how information may be collected and used.</p><h2>30. Changes to These Terms</h2><p>Green Alliance Enterprises may update these website Terms &amp; Conditions when required due to:</p><ul><li>Changes in project operations</li><li>Revised payment policies</li><li>Changes in facilities</li><li>Regulatory requirements</li><li>Government instructions</li><li>PAMRA requirements</li><li>Changes in applicable laws or company policies</li></ul><p>The latest version will be published on this website with an updated revision date.</p><p>For existing allottees, rights and obligations remain governed by their applicable signed agreements and official project documents.</p><h2>31. Governing Rules</h2><p>Project activities, market operations and allotments are subject to applicable laws and regulations in Pakistan and Punjab, together with relevant PAMRA requirements, company bylaws and official allotment agreements.</p><p>All market functionaries must follow any applicable regulatory rules issued or amended from time to time.</p><h2>32. Contact Green Alliance Enterprises</h2><p>For official information regarding bookings, commercial plots, payment schedules, possession or market operations, please contact:</p><p><strong>Green Alliance Enterprises</strong><br><strong>Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market</strong><br>Abbasia Chowk, 0.5 KM towards Bahawalpur Road<br>Opposite Javed CNG Pump<br>Ahmedpur East, Punjab, Pakistan</p><p><strong>Phone:</strong> 0303-3341200</p><p>Prospective buyers should obtain the latest official documents directly from Green Alliance Enterprises before making any payment.</p><h2>Important Disclaimer</h2><p>Information on this website is intended to provide a convenient overview of Green Alliance Enterprises and its commercial opportunities.</p><p><strong>The official signed Application Form, Allotment Agreement, Payment Schedule, Possession Documents and project Terms &amp; Conditions shall prevail over website content in the event of any inconsistency.</strong></p><p>Prospective investors and allottees are encouraged to carefully review all official documentation before booking or purchasing a commercial plot.</p>', '1', NULL, 'default', 'Welcome to the official website of Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market (“GAE”).', 'published', '2026-08-16 17:12:33', '2026-08-16 17:21:50'),
('18', 'Disclaimer', '<h1>Disclaimer</h1><p><strong>Last Updated: August 16, 2026</strong></p><p>This website has been developed for <strong>Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market (“GAE”)</strong> for informational, promotional, and general communication purposes.</p><p>Please read this Disclaimer carefully before relying upon any information, image, statement, price, payment plan, facility description, project specification, investment opportunity, or other material appearing on this website.</p><p>By accessing or using this website, you acknowledge and agree to the terms of this Disclaimer.</p><h2>1. Website Developer Is Not the Owner of Green Alliance Enterprises</h2><p>The individual, company, freelancer, agency, or technical service provider responsible for designing, developing, maintaining, administering, or technically managing this website (collectively referred to as the <strong>“Website Developer”</strong>) is <strong>not the owner of Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market</strong>.</p><p>The Website Developer has provided website design, development, technical, content-presentation, or related digital services only.</p><p>Unless expressly confirmed through a separate written authorization, the Website Developer is not:</p><ul><li>An owner or shareholder of Green Alliance Enterprises</li><li>A partner or joint-venture partner of GAE</li><li>A director or officer of GAE</li><li>A property owner</li><li>A real estate developer of the project</li><li>A commission agent or arhti</li><li>A property dealer or broker</li><li>An investment adviser</li><li>A financial adviser</li><li>An authorized sales representative</li><li>A guarantor of the project</li><li>A party to any allotment, booking, lease, sale, purchase, possession, or investment agreement</li></ul><p>Nothing appearing on this website should be interpreted as creating a partnership, joint venture, agency, fiduciary relationship, ownership relationship, or other legal relationship between the Website Developer and Green Alliance Enterprises beyond the technical or professional services actually provided.</p><h2>2. Green Alliance Enterprises Is Responsible for the Project</h2><p>All matters concerning the actual Green Alliance Enterprises project, including but not limited to:</p><ul><li>Ownership</li><li>Project development</li><li>Commercial plots or shops</li><li>Allotments</li><li>Bookings</li><li>Possession</li><li>Payment schedules</li><li>Installments</li><li>Refunds</li><li>Transfers</li><li>Development work</li><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Facilities</li><li>Regulatory approvals</li><li>Market operations</li><li>Commission-agent arrangements</li><li>Registration</li><li>Licence requirements</li><li>Project documentation</li><li>Prices and charges</li></ul><p>are matters between <strong>Green Alliance Enterprises, the relevant authorities, and the applicable customer, allottee, investor, trader, or other contracting party</strong>.</p><p>The Website Developer is not responsible for performing, guaranteeing, enforcing, or supervising any such obligation.</p><h2>3. Website Information Is Provided in Good Faith</h2><p>The information published on this website has been prepared and presented in good faith using information believed to be accurate at the time of publication, including information, documents, promotional material, photographs, specifications, and other details supplied or made available by Green Alliance Enterprises or related sources.</p><p>Every reasonable effort may be made to present information correctly; however, <strong>errors, omissions, outdated information, typographical mistakes, misunderstandings, formatting errors, or unintentional inaccuracies may occur</strong>.</p><p>Neither the Website Developer nor the website itself guarantees that every item of information displayed will always be complete, current, error-free, or suitable for a particular purpose.</p><h2>4. Always Verify Information With the Official GAE Team</h2><p>Visitors must <strong>independently confirm all important information directly with the authorized Green Alliance Enterprises team before making any booking, payment, purchase, investment, allotment, business, or legal decision</strong>.</p><p>This includes confirmation of:</p><ul><li>Plot or shop availability</li><li>Plot numbers</li><li>Plot and shop sizes</li><li>Prices</li><li>Down-payment requirements</li><li>Installment schedules</li><li>Possession terms</li><li>Development status</li><li>Project completion status</li><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Facilities</li><li>Electricity availability</li><li>Banking facilities</li><li>Roads</li><li>Auction platforms</li><li>Boundary walls</li><li>Sewerage</li><li>CCTV arrangements</li><li>Mosque or other amenities</li><li>Regulatory approvals</li><li>PAMRA-related information</li><li>Taxes and government charges</li><li>Documentation charges</li><li>Registration fees</li><li>Transfer fees</li><li>Cancellation conditions</li><li>Refund terms</li><li>Any other financial or contractual condition</li></ul><p><strong>Do not make a financial or property transaction solely on the basis of information displayed on this website.</strong></p><h2>5. Official Documents Take Priority</h2><p>Any information displayed on this website is secondary to official documentation issued or executed by Green Alliance Enterprises and the relevant authorities.</p><p>Where there is any difference, discrepancy, contradiction, or ambiguity between website content and official documentation, the applicable official documents shall take priority.</p><p>These may include:</p><ul><li>Application forms</li><li>Booking forms</li><li>Allotment letters</li><li>Payment schedules</li><li>Possession slips</li><li>Signed agreements</li><li>Lease documents</li><li>Transfer documents</li><li>Approved layout plans</li><li>Official authority approvals</li><li>Green Alliance Enterprises Terms &amp; Conditions</li><li>Government or regulatory documents</li></ul><p>Prospective customers and investors should carefully review these documents before entering into any transaction.</p><h2>6. PAMRA and Regulatory Information</h2><p>References on this website to <strong>PAMRA</strong>, regulatory approvals, registrations, approved plans, licences, government departments, WAPDA/electricity arrangements, or other authorities are presented on the basis of information or documentation supplied or represented in relation to the project.</p><p>Users must independently verify the latest status, scope, validity, conditions, and applicability of any approval or regulatory matter directly with Green Alliance Enterprises and, where appropriate, the relevant government or regulatory authority.</p><p>The Website Developer does not issue, certify, verify, renew, guarantee, or enforce any governmental or regulatory approval.</p><h2>7. Real and AI-Generated Images</h2><p>This website may contain a combination of:</p><ul><li>Actual photographs of the project or related activities</li><li>Photographs supplied by Green Alliance Enterprises</li><li>Stock or illustrative imagery</li><li>Digitally enhanced images</li><li>Computer-generated visuals</li><li>Artificial Intelligence (AI)-generated images</li><li>Conceptual or artistic representations</li></ul><p>Not every image displayed on this website necessarily represents the <strong>current physical condition, completed development, exact design, layout, appearance, scale, materials, landscaping, traffic, number of visitors, number of businesses, facilities, or future condition of the project</strong>.</p><h2>8. AI-Generated and Conceptual Visuals</h2><p>Some images may have been generated or enhanced using artificial intelligence or other visualization technologies.</p><p>Such images are intended solely to help visitors understand a <strong>possible, conceptual, promotional, or anticipated future appearance</strong> of the market.</p><p>AI-generated images should <strong>not</strong> be interpreted as:</p><ul><li>Photographic evidence of completed development</li><li>A guaranteed final appearance</li><li>An architectural commitment</li><li>An approved engineering drawing</li><li>An official site plan</li><li>A construction specification</li><li>A guarantee regarding future market activity</li><li>A representation of exact shop designs or infrastructure</li><li>A guarantee of customer traffic or commercial activity</li></ul><p>Actual development may differ significantly from conceptual or AI-generated visuals.</p><p>Visitors and investors should inspect the actual site and official plans before making decisions.</p><h2>9. Project Renderings Are Illustrative</h2><p>Any rendering, visualization, architectural concept, map, graphic, illustration, or promotional design displayed on this website should be considered <strong>illustrative unless expressly identified as an official approved document</strong>.</p><p>Elements shown in such visuals—including roads, buildings, shops, sheds, landscaping, vehicles, people, signage, lighting, facilities, and surrounding development—may differ from actual or final conditions.</p><h2>10. No Investment Advice</h2><p>Nothing on this website constitutes financial, investment, legal, tax, accounting, or professional investment advice.</p><p>References to:</p><ul><li>Investment opportunities</li><li>Commercial potential</li><li>Business growth</li><li>Shop ownership</li><li>Market demand</li><li>Future development</li><li>Regional business opportunities</li></ul><p>are general promotional or informational statements only.</p><p>Every prospective investor should independently assess the project, review official documentation, inspect the site, evaluate financial risks, and obtain independent professional advice where appropriate.</p><h2>11. No Guarantee of Profit or Investment Return</h2><p>Neither Green Alliance Enterprises\' website nor the Website Developer guarantees:</p><ul><li>Profit</li><li>Rental income</li><li>Capital appreciation</li><li>Resale value</li><li>Future demand</li><li>Customer footfall</li><li>Business turnover</li><li>Market occupancy</li><li>Return on investment</li><li>Business success</li><li>Future property value</li></ul><p>Every commercial investment carries its own risks, and users remain responsible for their individual investment and business decisions.</p><h2>12. No Guarantee Regarding Availability</h2><p>A plot, shop, unit, business location, payment plan, price, discount, facility, or offer displayed on this website may become unavailable, sold, reserved, withdrawn, modified, or changed.</p><p>Website information should therefore not be interpreted as a guarantee that a particular opportunity remains available.</p><p>Users must obtain current confirmation directly from the authorized GAE team.</p><h2>13. Prices and Payment Plans May Change</h2><p>Any reference to prices, installment periods, down payments, possession arrangements, charges, or other financial terms is subject to the official documentation applicable at the time of the transaction.</p><p>For example, references to a <strong>25% down payment, possession arrangements, or installment plans</strong> must always be confirmed against the latest official Green Alliance Enterprises documents before payment.</p><p>Website content alone does not create a right to any particular price, payment arrangement, possession date, or financial benefit.</p><h2>14. Website Developer Does Not Accept Responsibility for Transactions</h2><p>The Website Developer is not a party to transactions entered into between visitors and Green Alliance Enterprises or any other person.</p><p>Accordingly, to the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Website Developer shall not be responsible for disputes arising from:</p><ul><li>Payments</li><li>Deposits</li><li>Bookings</li><li>Installments</li><li>Allotments</li><li>Possession</li><li>Cancellations</li><li>Refunds</li><li>Transfers</li><li>Construction</li><li>Development delays</li><li>Documentation</li><li>Regulatory matters</li><li>Business operations</li><li>Representations made separately by sales representatives</li><li>Investor expectations</li><li>Property ownership disputes</li></ul><p>Such matters must be addressed with the relevant contracting party or authority.</p><h2>15. Do Not Make Payments to the Website Developer</h2><p>Unless Green Alliance Enterprises provides express written authorization for a specific transaction, visitors should <strong>not make booking, investment, installment, allotment, transfer, or property payments to the Website Developer</strong>.</p><p>Payments relating to Green Alliance Enterprises should only be made through the payment channels officially authorized by GAE and confirmed through official project documentation.</p><p>Visitors are responsible for verifying payment instructions before transferring money.</p><h2>16. No Authority to Make Commitments on Behalf of GAE</h2><p>Unless separately and expressly authorized in writing, the Website Developer has no authority to:</p><ul><li>Sell plots or shops</li><li>Confirm bookings</li><li>Guarantee availability</li><li>Alter prices</li><li>Approve refunds</li><li>Promise possession</li><li>Execute allotments</li><li>Accept contractual obligations</li><li>Modify GAE Terms &amp; Conditions</li><li>Guarantee regulatory approvals</li><li>Make legally binding commitments on behalf of Green Alliance Enterprises</li></ul><p>Statements made through website design or content should therefore not be treated as independent contractual promises by the Website Developer.</p><h2>17. Limitation of Website Developer Liability</h2><p>To the <strong>maximum extent permitted by applicable law</strong>, the Website Developer shall not be liable for any direct, indirect, incidental, consequential, special, commercial, financial, or other loss arising from reliance upon:</p><ul><li>Website content</li><li>Outdated information</li><li>Incorrect information provided by third parties</li><li>Project representations</li><li>Photographs</li><li>AI-generated images</li><li>Conceptual renderings</li><li>Prices</li><li>Investment information</li><li>Payment plans</li><li>Availability information</li><li>Links to external services</li><li>Technical errors</li><li>Website downtime</li><li>Unauthorized third-party modifications</li><li>User misunderstanding</li><li>Decisions made without independent verification</li></ul><p>Users access and use this website at their own discretion and are responsible for independently verifying material information before acting upon it.</p><p>Nothing in this Disclaimer is intended to exclude liability that cannot lawfully be excluded under applicable law.</p><h2>18. Information Supplied by Third Parties</h2><p>The Website Developer may rely upon information, documents, photographs, specifications, promotional statements, and other material supplied by Green Alliance Enterprises, its representatives, contractors, consultants, photographers, marketers, or other third parties.</p><p>The Website Developer is not responsible for independently auditing, surveying, valuing, legally verifying, engineering, certifying, or authenticating every item supplied for publication.</p><p>Responsibility for the underlying accuracy of third-party information remains with the appropriate source, subject to applicable law.</p><h2>19. Site Inspection Is Recommended</h2><p>Potential buyers, investors, traders, commission agents, and business owners are strongly encouraged to personally visit the Green Alliance Enterprises project site before making a transaction.</p><p>Visitors should compare:</p><ul><li>Actual site conditions</li><li>Available plots or shops</li><li>Roads</li><li>Trading areas</li><li>Auction platforms</li><li>Infrastructure</li><li>Existing facilities</li><li>Development progress</li></ul><p>with the official documents and representations supplied directly by GAE.</p><h2>20. Third-Party Links and Platforms</h2><p>This website may link to or integrate third-party services such as:</p><ul><li>Google Maps</li><li>WhatsApp</li><li>Facebook</li><li>Instagram</li><li>YouTube</li><li>Banks</li><li>Telephone services</li><li>External websites</li></ul><p>The Website Developer and Green Alliance Enterprises do not control every third-party platform.</p><p>Use of external services is subject to the applicable third party\'s own policies, terms, availability, and security practices.</p><h2>21. Technical Errors and Website Availability</h2><p>The Website Developer makes reasonable efforts to maintain the website; however, uninterrupted or error-free availability cannot be guaranteed.</p><p>The website may experience:</p><ul><li>Temporary downtime</li><li>Hosting problems</li><li>Software errors</li><li>Broken links</li><li>Browser compatibility issues</li><li>Server problems</li><li>Security incidents</li><li>Third-party service interruptions</li><li>Maintenance periods</li></ul><p>The Website Developer shall not, to the fullest extent permitted by law, be responsible for losses resulting solely from temporary technical unavailability or ordinary technical malfunction outside reasonable control.</p><h2>22. Website Content May Change Without Notice</h2><p>Website content may be added, modified, corrected, removed, or updated from time to time.</p><p>Changes may concern:</p><ul><li>Project information</li><li>Articles</li><li>Images</li><li>Facilities</li><li>Offers</li><li>Payment information</li><li>Contacts</li><li>Policies</li><li>Regulatory information</li><li>Marketing material</li></ul><p>Users should not assume that previously viewed website information remains current.</p><h2>23. No Reliance Without Independent Verification</h2><p>By using this website, you acknowledge that important financial, property, investment, or contractual decisions should not be based exclusively on website content.</p><p>Before entering into any transaction, users should:</p><ol><li>Contact the official GAE team.</li><li>Visit the project site.</li><li>Confirm current availability.</li><li>Review official payment schedules.</li><li>Review the official Terms &amp; Conditions.</li><li>Verify relevant approvals where necessary.</li><li>Obtain receipts for payments.</li><li>Review all contractual documents before signing.</li><li>Seek independent professional or legal advice where appropriate.</li></ol><h2>24. User Responsibility</h2><p>Every visitor, investor, customer, trader, or prospective buyer remains responsible for conducting appropriate due diligence before entering into any transaction.</p><p>Failure to independently verify information available through official channels remains the responsibility of the person making the transaction or decision, subject always to applicable law.</p><h2>25. No Waiver of Mandatory Legal Rights</h2><p>Nothing in this Disclaimer is intended to remove, restrict, or exclude any obligation or right that cannot legally be excluded under applicable law.</p><p>Where any provision of this Disclaimer conflicts with a mandatory legal requirement, that requirement shall prevail to the extent necessary.</p><h2>26. Severability</h2><p>If any provision of this Disclaimer is found by a competent authority or court to be invalid, unlawful, or unenforceable, that provision should be interpreted or limited to the minimum extent necessary, while the remaining provisions shall continue to apply to the extent permitted by law.</p><h2>27. Relationship With Other Website Policies</h2><p>This Disclaimer should be read together with the website\'s:</p><ul><li><strong>Terms &amp; Conditions</strong></li><li><strong>Privacy Policy</strong></li><li>Any applicable booking or allotment terms</li><li>Official Green Alliance Enterprises documentation</li></ul><p>Official signed transaction documents remain separate from general website information.</p><h2>28. Contact the Official Green Alliance Enterprises Team</h2><p>For confirmation of project information, commercial opportunities, prices, booking, payment schedules, possession, approvals, facilities, and other official matters, please contact Green Alliance Enterprises directly:</p><p><strong>Green Alliance Enterprises</strong><br><strong>Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market</strong><br>Abbasia Chowk, approximately 0.5 KM towards Bahawalpur Road<br>Opposite Javed CNG Pump<br>Ahmedpur East, Punjab, Pakistan</p><p><strong>Phone:</strong> 0303-3341200</p><h2>Final Disclaimer</h2><p><strong>The Website Developer is an independent website/technical service provider and is not the owner of Green Alliance Enterprises or the Green Alliance Enterprises Fruit &amp; Vegetable Market.</strong></p><p>Website information is presented in good faith and according to information reasonably available at the time of publication, but mistakes, omissions, outdated details, or inaccuracies may occur.</p><p>Some photographs displayed on this website are real, while other images may be AI-generated, digitally created, enhanced, conceptual, or illustrative. Such images may represent a possible future appearance and should not be considered evidence of the present or guaranteed final condition of the project.</p><p><strong>Before making any payment, booking, investment, purchase, allotment, or other commercial decision, visitors must verify all material information directly with the authorized Green Alliance Enterprises team and review the applicable official documentation.</strong></p><p>To the fullest extent permitted by applicable law, the Website Developer accepts no responsibility for property transactions, investments, payments, promises, representations, project development, possession, refunds, financial outcomes, or disputes between Green Alliance Enterprises and any customer, investor, allottee, trader, commission agent, or other third party.</p>', '1', NULL, 'default', 'Please read this Disclaimer carefully before relying upon any information, image, statement, price, payment plan, facility description, project specification, investment opportunity, or other material appearing on this website.', 'published', '2026-08-16 17:22:44', '2026-08-16 17:22:44');

-- Table structure for `pages_translations`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `pages_translations`;
CREATE TABLE `pages_translations` (
  `lang_code` varchar(20) NOT NULL,
  `pages_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL,
  `name` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `description` varchar(400) DEFAULT NULL,
  `content` longtext DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`lang_code`,`pages_id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `password_reset_tokens`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `password_reset_tokens`;
CREATE TABLE `password_reset_tokens` (
  `email` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `token` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`email`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `payment_logs`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `payment_logs`;
CREATE TABLE `payment_logs` (
  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `payment_method` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `request` longtext DEFAULT NULL,
  `response` longtext DEFAULT NULL,
  `ip_address` varchar(45) NOT NULL,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `updated_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `payments`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `payments`;
CREATE TABLE `payments` (
  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `currency` varchar(120) DEFAULT NULL,
  `user_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL DEFAULT 0,
  `charge_id` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `payment_channel` varchar(60) DEFAULT NULL,
  `description` varchar(400) DEFAULT NULL,
  `amount` decimal(15,2) unsigned NOT NULL,
  `payment_fee` decimal(15,2) DEFAULT 0.00,
  `order_id` bigint(20) unsigned DEFAULT NULL,
  `status` varchar(60) DEFAULT 'pending',
  `payment_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT 'confirm',
  `customer_id` bigint(20) unsigned DEFAULT NULL,
  `refunded_amount` decimal(15,2) unsigned DEFAULT NULL,
  `refund_note` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `updated_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `customer_type` varchar(255) DEFAULT NULL,
  `metadata` mediumtext DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `personal_access_tokens`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `personal_access_tokens`;
CREATE TABLE `personal_access_tokens` (
  `id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL AUTO_INCREMENT,
  `tokenable_type` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `tokenable_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL,
  `name` varchar(255) NOT NULL,
  `token` varchar(64) NOT NULL,
  `abilities` text DEFAULT NULL,
  `last_used_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `expires_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `created_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  `updated_at` timestamp NULL DEFAULT NULL,
  PRIMARY KEY (`id`),
  UNIQUE KEY `personal_access_tokens_token_unique` (`token`),
  KEY `personal_access_tokens_tokenable_type_tokenable_id_index` (`tokenable_type`,`tokenable_id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `post_categories`
DROP TABLE IF EXISTS `post_categories`;
CREATE TABLE `post_categories` (
  `category_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL,
  `post_id` bigint(20) unsigned NOT NULL,
  KEY `post_categories_category_id_index` (`category_id`),
  KEY `post_categories_post_id_index` (`post_id`)
) ENGINE=InnoDB DEFAULT CHARSET=utf8mb4 COLLATE=utf8mb4_unicode_ci;

-- Table structure for `post_tags`
